Subject: [PATCH] content: BarcodeDetector follows the claimed platform

Chrome exposes BarcodeDetector on macOS, Android and ChromeOS only, so a
page on real Windows or Linux Chrome finds none. The browser decides
this from the platform the profile claims instead of the machine it runs
on, and nothing changes without a profile. On a build other than macOS,
a macOS profile's detector lists no formats and rejects detect(),
because that host has no barcode service.

diff --git a/content/child/runtime_features.cc b/content/child/runtime_features.cc
--- a/content/child/runtime_features.cc
+++ b/content/child/runtime_features.cc
@@ -524,6 +524,17 @@
     }
   }
 
+  // BarcodeDetector follows the platform the profile claims. The json5 ships
+  // it on macOS, Android and ChromeOS only, so real Windows and Linux Chrome
+  // have no BarcodeDetector while real macOS Chrome does, whatever machine
+  // this build runs on. With no profile loaded nothing is touched.
+  if (const base::apostate::Profile* profile = base::apostate::Profile::Get()) {
+    if (const std::optional<std::string>& claimed = profile->ua_platform()) {
+      blink::WebRuntimeFeatures::EnableFeatureFromString("BarcodeDetector",
+                                                         *claimed == "macOS");
+    }
+  }
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
   if (base::android::android_info::sdk_int() <
       base::android::android_info::SDK_VERSION_P) {
